language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Choose how many units of each of four foods to buy so that every nutrition requirement is met at minimum cost.
given n : int
given price : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..1000000)
given limits : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..1000000)
$ the problem's table of nutrient content per unit (rows: calories, chocolate ounces, sugar ounces, fat ounces; columns: chocolate cake, ice cream, cola, cheesecake)
letting nutrient = [[400, 200, 150, 500], [3, 2, 0, 0], [2, 2, 4, 4], [2, 4, 1, 5]]
find units : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..max(limits))
find cost : int(0..10000000)

minimising cost
such that
$ the cost is the sum of the price of each food times the units bought
cost = (sum i : int(1..n) . price[i] * units[i]),
$ each nutrition type must reach at least its required limit
forAll j : int(1..n) . ((sum i : int(1..n) . nutrient[j,i] * units[i]) >= limits[j])
